{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '215,247p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792302000000-architect-antlr-multi-reconcile-r2.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md && cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792304000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-r3.prompt.md && cat docs/agents/roles/lead-system-architect.md\"","aggregated_output":"`{:rule-names #{...} :token-names #{...} :synthetic-policy {...}}`. It runs after\n`validate!`. Returns the packet or throws a qualified `malformed-cst` naming the first\nviolated invariant. `:rule-names` and `:token-names` come from the running host's generated\ntables (`cst/vocabulary worker`, §2.1); `:synthetic-policy` comes from the language's\nprofile (§1.3.1). The conformance helper (§5.2) assembles the map; `conform` itself is\nhost-free and language-free.\n\n#### 1.3.1 Synthetic policy: grammar role as data (new, finding 10)\n\nA grammar with lexer helpers constructs tokens that no source bytes produced (Python's\nDEDENT, the end-of-input NEWLINE, every grammar's EOF). Whether a token type may or must\nbe synthetic is a property of the grammar and its helper, so it is declared once per\nlanguage on the profile, not inferred from text:\n\n```clojure\n:synthetic-policy {\"NEWLINE\" :at-end, \"DEDENT\" :always}     ; Python3; INDENT is absent: never\n```\n\nValues: `:never` (the default for every type not listed, and for every real-text token\ntype such as NAME, NUMBER, ASSIGN, INDENT), `:always` (the helper constructs every token\nof this type; it is zero-width), `:at-end` (the helper constructs one at end of input;\nelsewhere the type is a real token). `\"EOF\"` is `:always` in every grammar and is merged in\nby `conform`; a language's policy need not list it. A grammar without helpers declares\nnothing.\n\nThe policy is grammar data in cljc, like `grammar-id`, so it is the same on every host and\nis written into the goldens file beside the vocabulary (§5.1). It is **not** read by the\nexporter: the exporter decides `:synthetic` from host-token evidence it alone has (char\nindexes, §2.1), the oracle decides from role; two independent derivations that must agree\non every golden. That is the \"independent host-token evidence or explicit grammar-specific\npolicy\" the reviewer asked for, supplied as both.\n\n#### 1.3.2 Checks for `:yang.cst/ok`\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-17 10:15:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 17:15:00 +07 (+0700)\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (capture thread.started; seat-assigned 96e4ab4e-8a2c-435d-87a0-e9ede52272c5)\n\n# Task: Re-review round 3 — the two P1 corrections in the antlr-multi plan\n\nRole: Lead System Architect (the same reviewer; the author's reconcile r2 routes back per protocol)\n\nTHE V3 PLAN (the delta from v2): /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792302000000-architect-antlr-multi-reconcile-r2.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md\n— the revised sections addressing your two P1s (the v2 for context:\ncollab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings-v2.md).\n\nVERIFY against your two repro-backed P1s:\n1. The synthetic-token justification: the :synthetic-policy map keyed on grammar role (NEWLINE :at-end,\n   DEDENT :always, EOF always, other types never); the oracle keys on type; the exporter keeps char-index\n   evidence; the goldens prove the two agree; the canonical synthetic text (empty, \"<EOF>\") removes the\n   runtime getText fallback; the one-edit change to the retained JVM exporter; the twelve-row mutation\n   table + three acceptance fixtures on every host. Your DEDENT {:text \"\" :span [16 16]} accepted; a\n   collapsed NAME rejected by type.\n2. The error coordinates: the span (source coordinates from char indexes with a boundary invariant) vs\n   ANTLR's line/column captured verbatim with bounds only — explicitly not required to agree; the cause\n   documented from the patched helper; the conformance corpus gains helper-NEWLINE/DEDENT error fixtures\n   pinned with their disagreeing coordinates as expected values. Your {:line 3 :column 0 :span [13 14]}\n   case handled.\n3. The original P1-class properties preserved (the §1.3.6 rewrite names which rule establishes each);\n   the ledger rows 10/11; nothing else regressed.\n\nVerdict: end with exactly one line \"Verdict: READY (sign-off granted)\" or \"Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES\" with\nfindings. Begin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT / Completed-Local\ncat: docs/agents/roles/lead-system-architect.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
