l targets and re-pins all digests in one commit (§4.2).\\n\\n## 4. The parser namespace per language\\n\\n`src/clj/yang/python/antlr/parser.clj` becomes\\n`src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc`:\\n\\n```clojure\\n(ns yang.python.antlr.parser\\n  (:require [yang.antlr.cst :as cst] [yang.stage :as stage]\\n            #?@(:clj [] :cljs [[\\\"antlr4\\\" :as antlr4]\\n                               [\\\"/yang/antlr/gen/python3/Python3Lexer.js\\\" :default Python3Lexer] ...]\\n                :cljd [[\\\"package:datomworld_cljd/antlr/python3/Python3Lexer.dart\\\" :as l] ...]))\\n  #?(:clj (:import (yang.python.antlr.gen Python3Lexer Python3Parser))))\\n\\n(def profile\\n  {:grammar-id grammar-id\\n   :make-lexer  #?(:clj (fn [cs] (Python3Lexer. cs)) :cljs (fn [cs] (Python3Lexer. cs)) :cljd (fn [cs] (l/Python3Lexer cs)))\\n   :make-parser ...\\n   :start       #?(:clj (fn [p] (.file_input p)) :cljs (fn [p] (.file_input p)) :cljd (fn [p] (.file_input p)))})\\n;; make-worker, parse-source, open-stage, step-stage unchanged\\n```\\n\\n`#?(:cljd ...)` must come first in each conditional (recorded trap). This file\\nis the entire per-language, per-host surface.\\n\\n## 5. CST equivalence: the parity story\\n\\nThree layers, all reusing existing tests by widening their host set:\\n\\n1. **Exporter conformance (per target, language-free)**: a new cljc\\n   `yang.antlr.conformance` test helper takes a profile and a fixture list\\n   `[source expected-shape]` and asserts, on the running host: packet\\n   `validate!` and `conform` pass; the `shape` (rule/type/text/span) equals the\\n   golden; spans are UTF-8 bytes (`\\\"s = 'é𝄞'\\\\nt = 2\\\\n\\\"` → `[4 12]`,\\n---\\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\\n---\\n\\n# BUILD & TEST\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```sh\\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \\\"name\\\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below for\\n# which lanes may overlap.\\n#\\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\\n# overlap lanes, see \\\"Remote test servers\\\" below).\\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\\n\\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n36:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_18\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT / Completed-Local\\n2026-10-17 13:05:51 GMT / 2026-10-17 20:05:51 +0700\\n\\nAll nine findings are conceded. The revisions address findings **2–9** at the design level: genuine full-packet goldens, absent-target composition, generation dependencies and classpaths, instance-owned caches, retirement prerequisites, browser acceptance, executable interoperability gates, and dependency provenance.\\n\\nFinding **1 remains partially unresolved**. The recursive preorder walk correctly rejects duplicate edges `[1 1 2]` and DFS order `[0 1 3 2]`; outcome-specific validation also admits legitimate error packets. However, the new conformance rules introduce two failures.\\n\\n1. **[P1] Synthetic-token justification rejects the required indentation golden.**  \\n   [v2:194–197](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings-v2.md:194) requires a synthetic token either to differ from source text at its position or to overlap the preceding real token.\\n\\n   Executing the existing JVM exporter on `\\\"if x:\\\\n    y = 1\\\\nz = 2\\\\n\\\"` produces:\\n\\n   ```clojure\\n   {:type \\\"DEDENT\\\" :text \\\"\\\" :span [16 16] :synthetic true}\\n   ```\\n\\n   The source slice is `\\\"\\\"`, and the preceding real NEWLINE ends at byte 16. Neither justification holds. Thus the indentation fixture expressly required by [v2:407–419](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings-v2.md:407) cannot pass M1.\\n\\n   The converse assurance is also too strong: collapsing a misplaced nonempty token to a zero-width span automatically makes its text differ from that empty source slice.\\n\\n   **Correction:** define justification for zero-width helper tokens separately from text mismatch. If detecting falsely synthetic tokens remains a promised property, supply independent host-token evidence or an explicit grammar-specific policy. Add both acceptance and mutation tests.\\n\\n2. **[P1] Error-coordinate conformance conflicts with the retained JVM exporter.**  \\n   [v2:199–201](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings-v2.md:199) requires listener line/column to identify the source position at span start. But [cst.clj:137–154](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-c4hang/src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj:137) computes spans from token indexes while retaining listener coordinates unchanged.\\n\\n   I reproduced this with `\\\"if x:\\\\n    y =\\\\nz = 2\\\\n\\\"`:\\n\\n   ```clojure\\n   {:line 3 :column 0 :span [13 14] ...}\\n   ```\\n\\n   Byte 13 is the newline on **line 2, column 7**. Message normalization in [v2:433–442](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings-v2.md:433) cannot resolve this mismatch.\\n\\n   **Correction:** explicitly choose canonical source-derived coordinates and update all exporters before generating JVM goldens, or specify a separate contract for listener coordinates. Include errors on helper-produced NEWLINE and DEDENT tokens.\\n\\nReview was read-only. I executed focused JVM exporter probes against existing generated classes; the proposed validators and JS/Dart implementations do not yet exist and were not executed.\\n\\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\"}}\n(ns yang.python.antlr.parser\n  \"The Python parser interpreter (JVM host): the grammars-v4 Python3 grammar\n   profile plus the stage that reads sealed source units from one stream and\n   writes CST packets to another. The generated recognizers come from\n   `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); this is the only\n   namespace that names them.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.stage :as stage])\n  (:import\n    (yang.python.antlr.gen\n      Python3Lexer\n      Python3Parser)))\n\n\n(def grammar-id\n  \"grammars-v4 python/python3 at its pinned revision, generated by ANTLR 4.13.2.\"\n  \"grammars-v4/python/python3@8af0d4c26c796ea27c15c3d85418f2d0f77c3adb antlr-4.13.2\")\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:grammar-id grammar-id,\n   :make-lexer (fn [cs] (Python3Lexer. cs)),\n   :make-parser (fn [ts] (Python3Parser. ts)),\n   :start (fn [^Python3Parser p] (.file_input p))})\n\n\n(defn make-worker\n  []\n  (cst/make-worker profile))\n\n\n(defn parse-source\n  \"Parse one complete source string as unit `unit`: the packet a sealed unit\n   with this text produces.\"\n  ([source] (parse-source (make-worker) [:unit 0] source))\n  ([worker unit source] (cst/parse-unit worker unit source)))\n\n\n(defn open-stage\n  \"A parser stage reading source events from `source-stream` and writing\n   CST packets to `cst-stream`, with its own worker.\"\n  [source-stream cst-stream]\n  (assoc (stage/open source-stream {:cst cst-stream} {})\n         ::transform (cst/parse-transform (make-worker))))\n\n\n(defn step-stage\n  [s]\n  (stage/step s (::transform s)))\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl.main/-main\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yang.python-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_A